  "prefLabel": "Lab 1002.03 Hours Limitations",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-08-02",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 1002.03 Hours Limitations.\n\n(a) As used in RSA 276-A: 4, IV the term \"vacations\" shall not include any week in which school is in session for one or more days.\n\n(b) Pursuant to RSA 276-A: 4, IV, no youth under 16 years of age shall work earlier than 7 o'clock a.m. or later than 9 o'clock p.m.\n\n(c) Pursuant to RSA 276-A:13, any youth scheduled to work more than 2 nights in a week past 8 o'clock p.m. shall not be permitted to work more than an 8-hour shift during that particular week.\n\nSource. #7337, eff 8-2-00; EXPIRED: 8-2-08\n\nNew. #9258, eff 9-11-08; ss by #10931, eff 9-15-15; ss by #13222, eff 6-26-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab1000.html"
